From 6ec72109701bd4c7d7bd0ac2814ce1bb7a51ea3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:28:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Transport: Close the connection of a failed TLS or REALITY
 handshake

When a handshake failed with an error of its own, such as a server that
answers with something other than TLS as a block page does, the RAW,
WebSocket, HTTPUpgrade and XHTTP dialers and the REALITY client returned
the error and left the connection open until the garbage collector found
it. They now close it; the REALITY client still hands an unverified
connection to its spider. A handshake cut by its context was closed by
crypto/tls and uTLS already.

HTTPUpgrade with "unsafe" or an unknown fingerprint took crypto/tls,
whose handshake ran on the first write with no bound, so a server that
took the ClientHello and answered nothing held the dial forever. It now
runs in the dial, under its context.

TestDialClosesTheConnectionOfAFailedHandshake dials each transport with
uTLS, crypto/tls and REALITY against a server that answers nothing or
answers HTTP, with the garbage collector off: 7 cases kept the connection
open before, and the HTTPUpgrade crypto/tls one hung.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
